  "notes": "Opened the actual frame-0 plate (1360x900) and the BiRefNet initial mask overlay at 4-8x. The initial mask included the gaming-chair backrest on BOTH sides of his head as solid foreground (two wedges, roughly x445-556 and x784-882, y256-500). Measured the chair edges from luma on this frame only: outer chair/wall edge 450-485 left and 850-875 right; inner skin edge from the ear down the cheek, jaw, beard and neck; shoulder/shirt top edge per column (left 503 at x455 rising to 462 at x540; right ~500-527). Wrote two exclude polygons that sit 3-4px on the chair side of every skin edge and 4px above the shoulder line, so cap, forehead, both ears, jaw, beard, neck and both shoulders are untouched. Re-inspected the corrected mask as a composite and as 4-8x crops of both chair zones, plus the cap crown, both hands and the bottom-left arm: both ears fully intact, no jaw or cheek carving, both hands and all fingertips still inside with margin, chair fully outside the contour on both sides, no leftover chair column at the right outer edge. 28205 px removed, foreground 43.4 -> 41.1 percent. Coordinates measured on this recording only.",
